well it's the homecoming we've been  waiting to share with you a las vegas  man who came to the u.s after working as  an interpreter for the u.s military in  afghanistan finally reunites with his  wife he says people reached out to help  him after we first interviewed him it's  an exclusive you'll only see on eight  news now  [Music]  this is what an embrace after a long  journey looks like for heck matt gauzy  and his wife laylee they still don't  believe that she's here it's the first  time they've seen each other in six  months they married a year ago in  afghanistan and honeymoon six months ago  in dubai but hekmat had to return to las  vegas without her until she get the  proper documentation to enter the united  states  the taliban takeover in august brought  with it great urgency and fear as laylee  had to remain in hiding i'm making  attempts to get in the airport and going  through thousands of people and shots  being fired people being beaten this  photo showing the relief as laylee and  her brother learned they are on a  special flight out of kabul from there  to qatar and then fort mccoy in  wisconsin she spends several weeks at an  integration training program for afghan  refugees the evening she flies into las  vegas hekmat learned that laylee's  father has passed away like it was a  mixed feeling you know it's like i lost  a father figure  and now i'm responsible for the family  that's left back there he and laylee  continue efforts to help other afghan  refugees and interpreters with the  non-profit freedom support alliance  which he runs with his friend bahir  shirzad we're actually working for the  afghan community here to help them you  know for the better future  lely is here on an immigrant visa as a  spouse of a u.s citizen freedom support  alliance has partnered with concerned  veterans of america to host a community  event for all afghans october 8 helping  them connect with resources in our area  and assist if they're looking for a job
 

